# HTML never goes stale on devices (tablet/phone cache bugs) — always revalidate.
#
# Security headers live in this same /* block rather than a second one: Cloudflare applies every
# matching rule, but two blocks with the same pattern is ambiguous to read and invites someone to
# "fix" the duplicate by deleting the wrong one.
#
# ⚠ Permissions-Policy deliberately does NOT include `payment=()`. That would disable the Payment
# Request API and kill Apple Pay / Google Pay the moment checkout moves from a Stripe redirect to
# embedded Elements. On a site whose whole job is taking payment, that is the wrong default.
#
# ⚠ No full Content-Security-Policy. These pages carry inline <script> and inline styles
# throughout, so any CSP that actually loaded would need `unsafe-inline` — which buys nothing.
# Doing it properly means a nonce/hash pass in build-nav.mjs first. `frame-ancestors` is set on
# its own because it is the clickjacking control and costs nothing to get right today.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()

# hashed/versioned static assets + media: cache long (query-param versioning governs JS)
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
